  "title": "Programmatically Control Subscription Offer Targeting",
  "summary": "Developers can now activate and deactivate targeting for specific subscription offers via new API methods, providing more dynamic control over promotional campaigns.",
  "details": "Two significant new methods have been added to the `purchases.subscriptionsv2` resource: `activateoffertargeting` and `deactivateoffertargeting`. These allow you to programmatically manage which specific offers are targeted for a given subscription. Both methods require `packageName` and `purchaseToken` as path parameters. The request bodies, `ActivateOfferTargetingRequest` and `DeactivateOfferTargetingRequest`, each require an `offerId` to specify the discounted offer. This update also introduces the `DeveloperTargetedOffer` schema to represent information about these offers, and adds an `etag` property to `CancellationContext` and `RevocationContext` for conditional operations, enhancing robustness.",
